   DECISION (FINAL): rewrite the link section of DeltaComplex.lean with the correct pair-based machinery:
   1. Link of a vertex class C: 
      - linkVertexClasses: Finset of classes of pairs (Corner, edge = 2-corner-set with the corner in it): computed via componentsOf with pairs generated by face gluings: for gluing (t,i)→(t',g): for j ≠ i, k ≠ i, j ≠ k: (⟨t,j⟩, {⟨t,j⟩,⟨t,k⟩}) ~ (⟨t',g j⟩, {⟨t',g j⟩,⟨t',g k⟩}).
      - linkEdgeClasses: classes of (face (t,i), corner j ≠ i) pairs: for gluing (t,i)→(t',g): (⟨t,i⟩,⟨t,j⟩) ~ (⟨t',g i⟩,⟨t',g j⟩) for j ≠ i.
      - link faces: the corners (t,j) ∈ C.
      - checks: each face: 3 distinct edge classes, 3 distinct vertex classes: each edge class in exactly 2 faces: connected (via shared edges): χ = V-E+F = 2 (sphere) or 1 (disk with boundary cycle conditions).
   2. Link of an edge class E (the CORRECT edge link): vertices = classes of (face, edge-occurrence) pairs [(t,i,{a,b}) with {a,b} ∈ E, i ∉ {a,b}]: arcs = classes of (tet, edge-occurrence) pairs [(t,{a,b}) with {a,b} ∈ E]: arc (t,{a,b}) connects the two face-occurrences (t,i,{a,b}), (t,i',{a,b}) where {i,i',a,b} = {0,1,2,3}: identifications from gluings: for gluing (t,i)→(t',g): (t,i,{a,b}) ~ (t',g i,{g a, g b}) [a,b ≠ i]: and (t,{a,b}) ~ (t',{g a, g b}): cycle: connected, every vertex 2 arcs, every arc 2 distinct endpoints, V - A = 0: path: exactly 2 vertices with 1 arc, rest 2, connected, V - A = 1.

   Then: IsCombinatorialManifoldWithBoundary: Consistent ∧ OrientationReversing ∧ (vertex classes: disk if boundary vertex else sphere) ∧ (edge classes: path if boundary edge else cycle) ∧ boundary = closed surface (χ = 2 per sphere component or 0 per torus; our examples: B³: sphere χ=2; solid torus: torus χ=0). And IsCombinatorialManifold (closed): Consistent ∧ OrientationReversing ∧ Closed ∧ all vertex links spheres ∧ all edge links cycles.

