  (edgeLinkArcs T E).filter (fun arc =>
    (List.finRange 4).filter (fun i => i ≠ arc.a ∧ i ≠ arc.b) |>.any (fun i =>
      (⟨⟨arc.t, i⟩, arc.a, arc.b⟩ : FaceOcc N) ∈ f)).length
```
Hmm: the degree: the number of HALF-EDGES: for each arc occurrence: its 2 adjacent face occurrences: the count of those in the class f: the filter: the arcs: each arc: 2 face-occs: `any` on the 2: counts the arc ONCE even if both face-occs ∈ f: WRONG: should count the number of face-occs in f: `(List.finRange 4).filter (fun i => i ≠ arc.a ∧ i ≠ arc.b ∧ (⟨⟨arc.t, i⟩, arc.a, arc.b⟩ : FaceOcc N) ∈ f).length` summed over arcs: so:

```lean
def edgeLinkDegree (T : FacePairing3 N) (E : Finset (Corner N)) (f : Finset (FaceOcc N)) : ℕ :=
  (edgeLinkArcs T E).map (fun arc =>
    (List.finRange 4).filter (fun i => i ≠ arc.a ∧ i ≠ arc.b ∧
      (⟨⟨arc.t, i⟩, arc.a, arc.b⟩ : FaceOcc N) ∈ f).length).sum
```

The connectivity: the componentsOf over the face classes with the pairs from the arcs' endpoint classes:
```lean
def edgeLinkConnected (T : FacePairing3 N) (E : Finset (Corner N)) : Prop :=
  let fcs := T.edgeLinkFaceClasses E
  let pairs : List (Finset (FaceOcc N) × Finset (FaceOcc N)) :=
    (edgeLinkArcs T E) =>> fun arc =>
      match (List.finRange 4).filter (fun i => i ≠ arc.a ∧ i ≠ arc.b) with
      | [i1, i2] => [((T.edgeLinkFaceClassOf E (⟨⟨arc.t, i1⟩, arc.a, arc.b⟩)),
                      (T.edgeLinkFaceClassOf E (⟨⟨arc.t, i2⟩, arc.a, arc.b⟩)))]
      | _ => []
  (componentsOf fcs pairs).card = 1
```
